## Monitoring

forge monitors this app{{if .DeclaredEnvs}} in {{range $i, $e := .DeclaredEnvs}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$e}}`{{end}}{{end}}: the app exports OpenTelemetry (traces, logs, metrics) to Reliant with a per-env ingest token, and forge reads it back. It needs a signed-in forge: under Reliant it already is; standalone, `{{.CLI}} login` (or a token in CI). Dashboards: https://forge.reliantlabs.io/forge/p/{{.Name}}/observability.

```bash
{{.CLI}} obs status <env>          # what is wrong now
{{.CLI}} obs issues <env>          # grouped errors, new and regressed
{{.CLI}} obs logs <env>            # logs; `obs traces` and `obs metrics` beside it
{{.CLI}} obs check <env> --json    # judge the newest service.version; branch on its exit code
```

With no deploy recorded, `obs check` dates a release from the first telemetry carrying its new `service.version`, and labels that marker INFERRED. Load `observability`, and `observability/query` for flags, documents and exit codes.
